  "methodology": "Two Bun WSS clients on the same local monotonic clock. One mover generates harmless inputs as each 60 Hz deadline arrives, checked by a 1 ms timer, recording actual creation time separately from nominal deadline and actual send time. Batch 3 retains each generated frame until the third; batch 1 sends immediately. Observer stays still; no firing, terrain changes, resets or deployment. Delayed timer callbacks catch up elapsed deadlines and may generate multiple frames together; generation intervals report this limitation. Ping is application RTT. Send-to-ack and send-to-observer measure first received snapshot with lastSeq >= input seq. Generated-to-observer also includes the measured client batching wait. Browser interpolation/render/display are excluded; this is not input-to-photon. Different sequential sessions have different snapshot phases and cannot establish an exact universal latency improvement.",
